 "method": "Power ranking (through the week): a weighted blend of z-scores --\n45% win percentage, 35% point differential per game, 20% the repo's\ndata-driven power model (power_model.py, fit on every game so far) once\nthere are enough games to fit it, else yardage differential per game.\n\nUnit rankings (through the week, per game with stats logged): each unit's\nstats turned into z-scores across the league and added up --\n  Quarterbacks:     passing yards + passing TD - interceptions + QBR/2\n  Receiving corps:  receiving yards + receiving TD + receptions/2\n  Defense:          - points allowed + sacks + interceptions\n                    + (tackles + swats + defensive TD)/2\n\nPlayer rankings (season totals through the week, top 5 each):\n  Quarterbacks:  passing yards + 20 x passing TD - 25 x interceptions\n  Receivers:     receiving yards + 20 x receiving TD\n  Defenders:     tackles + 4 x sacks + 5 x interceptions + 2 x swats\n                 + 10 x defensive TD\n\nNext week's predictions (from every game through the week): each team's\nexpected points = league average + its scoring edge (points scored per\ngame above average) + the opponent's defensive leak (points allowed per\ngame above average), each shrunk toward average for teams with few games\n(weight = games / (games + 2)), then tilted 1.5 points per unit of power\nscore difference. Win probability = normal CDF of the predicted margin\nover the league's spread of game margins so far. No home-field bonus.\n"
}